      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e How does the linker deal with overlapping expressions?\n\nI believe it uses the first match, and you\u0027re correct, .text.cfi is redundant here. The point is just to make sure all text sections are combined, so it doesn\u0027t matter whether TEXT_MAIN or TEXT_CFI_MAIN matches.\n\n\u003e Does .text.cfi need to be .text..cfi?\n\nThe section name is determined by the compiler and we can\u0027t change it. However, with LD_DEAD_CODE_DATA_ELIMINATION, .text.cfi won\u0027t be generated at all and each function will have a separate section instead.",
